1
00:00:25,959 --> 00:00:28,193
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,536 --> 00:00:38,336
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:51,416
♪ ♪

4
00:01:08,869 --> 00:01:10,346
<i>Okay, picture this.</i>

5
00:01:10,370 --> 00:01:13,138
We're close on an alarm clock...
- 15 a.m.

6
00:01:13,173 --> 00:01:15,606
Goes off, we pull back,
see a young woman...

7
00:01:15,642 --> 00:01:17,586
Yuppie, attractive,
hit the deck running.

8
00:01:17,610 --> 00:01:18,822
Then it quick cuts, we see

9
00:01:18,846 --> 00:01:20,223
an aerobics class,
business meetings,

10
00:01:20,247 --> 00:01:22,491
high-level confabs
with guys in suits.

11
00:01:22,515 --> 00:01:25,583
After work, racquetball,
dinner with friends.

12
00:01:25,618 --> 00:01:27,330
Then, back to her
setting the alarm clock

13
00:01:27,354 --> 00:01:28,698
while we hear a voice-over say,

14
00:01:28,722 --> 00:01:32,958
"Uniwear Bras: for
the active life you live."

15
00:01:32,993 --> 00:01:34,559
Tell me he's kidding.

16
00:01:35,829 --> 00:01:38,529
This campaign is geared
toward female boomers,

17
00:01:38,565 --> 00:01:39,864
women who never stop running.

18
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:40,865
Thanks.

19
00:01:40,901 --> 00:01:42,133
Now I get it.

20
00:01:42,169 --> 00:01:45,270
We are telling women we
have a bra they can sweat in?

21
00:01:45,306 --> 00:01:46,738
Where's the sex?

22
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:48,552
I deliberately focused
away from the sex.

23
00:01:48,576 --> 00:01:50,086
Women want to know
how this product...

24
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,609
Women want men.

25
00:01:51,645 --> 00:01:54,279
They want to find them,
catch them and keep them.

26
00:01:54,314 --> 00:01:56,981
They want to be pert
and perky for men,

27
00:01:57,017 --> 00:01:59,284
because men are
their real business.

28
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:00,952
Where did you get this idiot?

29
00:02:03,356 --> 00:02:05,690
Will you excuse us
for a minute, Edward?

30
00:02:05,725 --> 00:02:08,004
I would be glad to
rethink this, Mr. Howell.

31
00:02:08,028 --> 00:02:09,772
Give me a break. Look,

32
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:12,664
I was in the top 10% of my
class at Vanderbilt, Mr. Gordon.

33
00:02:12,699 --> 00:02:15,367
Well, you just flunked
out in the real world, pal.

34
00:02:15,402 --> 00:02:17,502
That is fine.

35
00:02:22,209 --> 00:02:23,508
Very nice.

36
00:02:23,544 --> 00:02:25,355
You think these
people don't talk?

37
00:02:25,379 --> 00:02:27,279
It's all over the business.

38
00:02:27,314 --> 00:02:29,226
How are we going to get good,

39
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:30,460
creative talent in here

40
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:32,161
if you treat people like that?

41
00:02:32,185 --> 00:02:34,586
By overpaying, the
way you do now.

42
00:02:34,622 --> 00:02:35,732
Yes?

43
00:02:35,756 --> 00:02:37,055
Get my wife, please.

44
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:38,824
You're hurting business, Alex.

45
00:02:38,859 --> 00:02:40,425
It's got to stop.

46
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:41,692
Buy me out.

47
00:02:41,728 --> 00:02:43,861
You'll lose the only
clown in this circus

48
00:02:43,897 --> 00:02:46,764
who knows how to write
a decent line of ad copy.

49
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,066
Hi, honey.

50
00:02:48,101 --> 00:02:49,812
Hi.

51
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:51,035
How's your day?

52
00:02:51,071 --> 00:02:52,471
Oh, lousy.

53
00:02:52,506 --> 00:02:54,251
We've got nothing for the
Uniwear meeting tomorrow,

54
00:02:54,275 --> 00:02:56,275
and I'm going to
be working all night.

55
00:02:57,678 --> 00:02:58,977
Are you staying in town?

56
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,012
Yeah.

57
00:03:00,047 --> 00:03:01,313
I'll be staying at the motel.

58
00:03:01,348 --> 00:03:02,981
Okay.

59
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:04,416
Good luck.

60
00:03:04,451 --> 00:03:05,584
Thanks.

61
00:03:08,688 --> 00:03:11,256
Pulling your fat out of
the fire again, buddy.

62
00:03:11,291 --> 00:03:12,691
Okay.

63
00:03:12,726 --> 00:03:15,960
Okay, if you want
to be a martyr.

64
00:03:15,995 --> 00:03:17,829
I'll see you tomorrow.

65
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:18,963
Martyr.

66
00:03:18,998 --> 00:03:20,332
Either I come up with something

67
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:21,533
for the Uniwear meeting

68
00:03:21,568 --> 00:03:24,869
or we go in with nothing
but our nervous smiles.

69
00:03:42,689 --> 00:03:44,223
Where is that report?

70
00:03:44,258 --> 00:03:45,757
You were in with Mr. Howell.

71
00:03:45,792 --> 00:03:47,859
I asked you to
type it an hour ago.

72
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:49,928
I did. I didn't want
to disturb you.

73
00:03:49,963 --> 00:03:52,197
Bring it. Bring it.

74
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:54,899
Okay. I'll see you in
five minutes, all right?

75
00:04:01,909 --> 00:04:03,842
♪ ♪

76
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:35,873
♪ ♪

77
00:04:54,627 --> 00:04:57,162
Anything else you
need, Mr. Gordon?

78
00:04:57,197 --> 00:04:58,496
A good night's sleep.

79
00:04:58,531 --> 00:04:59,742
Give me a wake-up call

80
00:04:59,766 --> 00:05:01,844
at 7:00 a.m., will
you, John? Sure thing.

81
00:05:01,868 --> 00:05:03,068
Hold your calls till then?

82
00:05:03,103 --> 00:05:04,736
Except for my wife.

83
00:05:04,771 --> 00:05:05,870
You got it.

84
00:05:05,906 --> 00:05:07,706
Sleep well, Mr. Gordon.

85
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:17,082
♪ ♪

86
00:05:55,055 --> 00:05:56,721
Come!

87
00:06:26,753 --> 00:06:28,687
♪ ♪

88
00:07:24,845 --> 00:07:26,778
♪ ♪

89
00:08:18,598 --> 00:08:20,531
♪ ♪

90
00:08:47,794 --> 00:08:49,728
♪ ♪

91
00:09:18,725 --> 00:09:20,658
♪ ♪

92
00:09:58,364 --> 00:10:00,298
♪ ♪

93
00:10:31,097 --> 00:10:32,963
Alex?

94
00:11:02,995 --> 00:11:04,929
♪ ♪

95
00:11:29,155 --> 00:11:31,055
I told you... no interruptions.

96
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:32,768
I'm sorry, sir, but
the police are here,

97
00:11:32,792 --> 00:11:33,936
and they say it's important.

98
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,592
The police?

99
00:11:45,305 --> 00:11:46,882
I'm sorry to disturb
you, Mr. Gordon.

100
00:11:46,906 --> 00:11:49,106
Lieutenant Brooks, Atlanta PD.

101
00:11:49,142 --> 00:11:50,541
What can I do for you?

102
00:11:50,576 --> 00:11:52,487
Well, there was a
problem at your house,

103
00:11:52,511 --> 00:11:55,213
and, uh, we'd like for you
to come with us if you can.

104
00:11:55,248 --> 00:11:56,681
What happened?

105
00:11:56,717 --> 00:11:58,728
I'm sorry to have
to tell you like this,

106
00:11:58,752 --> 00:12:00,852
but your wife...

107
00:12:00,887 --> 00:12:03,454
When the maid
came this morning...

108
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:05,801
Your wife is dead, sir.

109
00:12:05,825 --> 00:12:08,493
It appears she was
murdered last night.

110
00:12:12,432 --> 00:12:14,331
Now, we...

111
00:12:14,367 --> 00:12:17,502
we're trying to find
out all that we can.

112
00:12:19,005 --> 00:12:20,438
Murdered?

113
00:12:20,473 --> 00:12:22,307
Who?

114
00:12:22,342 --> 00:12:23,541
Oh, dear God.

115
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:24,675
Ca-Cathy?

116
00:12:24,710 --> 00:12:26,010
Somebody killed Cathy?

117
00:12:26,045 --> 00:12:28,412
We're hoping that you
can help us find out.

118
00:12:28,447 --> 00:12:31,516
A burgundy Jaguar was seen
near your house last night.

119
00:12:31,551 --> 00:12:33,618
Do you know anyone
with a car like that?

120
00:12:33,653 --> 00:12:35,186
No.

121
00:12:36,756 --> 00:12:39,190
Burgundy. My-my partner's...

122
00:12:39,225 --> 00:12:40,525
What's his name?

123
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:43,027
Bret Howell, but...

124
00:12:43,062 --> 00:12:46,096
he wouldn't have been
anywhere near there last night.

125
00:12:47,534 --> 00:12:48,599
I'm sorry.

126
00:12:48,635 --> 00:12:50,068
I must go home.

127
00:12:50,103 --> 00:12:52,937
Of course. Uh, we'll
take you there right away.

128
00:12:55,842 --> 00:12:58,910
<i>I didn't plan to fall
in love with Cathy,</i>

129
00:12:58,945 --> 00:13:01,279
nor she with me.

130
00:13:01,314 --> 00:13:04,082
For a long time,
we were just friends.

131
00:13:04,117 --> 00:13:05,983
She was so beautiful,

132
00:13:06,018 --> 00:13:07,719
so intelligent.

133
00:13:07,754 --> 00:13:09,654
Who'd want to kill her?

134
00:13:09,689 --> 00:13:13,191
Well, the police think you did.

135
00:13:13,226 --> 00:13:16,728
And you were seen going
into the house last night.

136
00:13:16,763 --> 00:13:18,662
Alex was staying in town.

137
00:13:18,698 --> 00:13:21,733
Cathy and I knew we'd
have some time together.

138
00:13:21,768 --> 00:13:24,035
When I left, she was fine.

139
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:25,703
And what time was that?

140
00:13:25,738 --> 00:13:28,439
About 11:45.

141
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:30,508
I...

142
00:13:34,514 --> 00:13:37,582
If I would have stayed,
she'd still be alive.

143
00:13:37,617 --> 00:13:39,884
Um, any idea how
the murder weapon

144
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,452
got in the trunk of your car?

145
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:42,720
No.

146
00:13:42,755 --> 00:13:45,155
Anybody else have a key?

147
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:50,027
Spare? In the office.

148
00:13:50,062 --> 00:13:51,896
Maybe at home, too.

149
00:14:01,274 --> 00:14:02,573
I, uh...

150
00:14:02,609 --> 00:14:06,143
I'm going to be honest
with you, Mr. Howell.

151
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:09,848
The district attorney
has a<i> very</i> strong case.

152
00:14:09,883 --> 00:14:12,050
I didn't do it, Mr. Matlock.

153
00:14:12,085 --> 00:14:15,419
I loved her.

154
00:14:15,455 --> 00:14:17,088
You believe me, don't you?

155
00:14:17,123 --> 00:14:20,725
I have to go under
that assumption.

156
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:23,294
But I-I-I...

157
00:14:23,329 --> 00:14:25,563
I don't have a clue

158
00:14:25,599 --> 00:14:28,165
how I'm going to
convince the jury

159
00:14:28,201 --> 00:14:32,003
that a man who's
sleeping with a woman...

160
00:14:32,038 --> 00:14:35,607
And not just any woman...
His partner's wife...

161
00:14:35,642 --> 00:14:38,676
And in his partner's house...

162
00:14:38,712 --> 00:14:42,346
Is a person of, uh,
high moral standards.

163
00:14:54,527 --> 00:14:56,138
Well, the maid
walked in this morning

164
00:14:56,162 --> 00:14:57,340
and nearly had a coronary.

165
00:14:57,364 --> 00:14:58,596
I guess.

166
00:14:58,631 --> 00:14:59,864
She have a key?

167
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,510
Yep, and the alarm code.

168
00:15:01,534 --> 00:15:02,833
The alarm was on?

169
00:15:02,869 --> 00:15:04,013
No, it was off.

170
00:15:04,037 --> 00:15:06,115
That's how the maid
knew something was wrong.

171
00:15:06,139 --> 00:15:07,616
Cathy Gordon
always set the alarm

172
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:09,873
just before she went to sleep.

173
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:13,111
She couldn't last night
when your client left.

174
00:15:13,146 --> 00:15:14,679
She was dead.

175
00:15:14,714 --> 00:15:16,325
Why do you say
"when your client left"?

176
00:15:16,349 --> 00:15:17,581
Well, it must have been him.

177
00:15:17,617 --> 00:15:19,094
Anyone else
coming in after he left

178
00:15:19,118 --> 00:15:20,451
would have set off the alarm.

179
00:15:20,486 --> 00:15:22,520
What about her husband?

180
00:15:22,555 --> 00:15:26,024
Well, I guess you're not
quite up to speed on this.

181
00:15:26,059 --> 00:15:28,926
He, uh, has an alibi
at a downtown motel.

182
00:15:28,961 --> 00:15:30,461
Stayed the night.

183
00:15:30,497 --> 00:15:33,197
But even without the alibi,
he couldn't have done it.

184
00:15:33,232 --> 00:15:34,464
Let's hear it.

185
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:37,060
Come on, I'll show you.

186
00:15:38,738 --> 00:15:41,172
See the contraption on
the stairs on your way up?

187
00:15:41,207 --> 00:15:42,518
Yeah. Yeah. It's broken.

188
00:15:42,542 --> 00:15:44,887
Six months. CONRAD: Yeah?

189
00:15:44,911 --> 00:15:46,322
Well, it's the only
way Mr. Gordon

190
00:15:46,346 --> 00:15:48,357
can get up and down the stairs.

191
00:15:48,381 --> 00:15:51,415
He's a paraplegic.

192
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:53,384
I didn't know that.

193
00:15:55,488 --> 00:15:57,088
Uh, anything else?

194
00:15:57,123 --> 00:15:58,556
There's a lot of blood.

195
00:15:58,591 --> 00:16:00,903
Yeah. Did you find any
clothes the killer was wearing?

196
00:16:00,927 --> 00:16:02,671
No. Anything taken?

197
00:16:02,695 --> 00:16:04,595
Nothing so far.

198
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:08,633
They got a good case.

199
00:16:08,668 --> 00:16:09,967
Yeah, they do.

200
00:16:10,002 --> 00:16:11,869
We're best friends
of the family.

201
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:16,106
Mr. Gordon's expecting us.

202
00:16:16,142 --> 00:16:17,853
It's okay, Officer.

203
00:16:17,877 --> 00:16:19,744
Thank you.

204
00:16:19,779 --> 00:16:21,846
Alex.

205
00:16:21,881 --> 00:16:23,648
We're so sorry.

206
00:16:26,786 --> 00:16:29,553
I can't believe it.

207
00:16:29,588 --> 00:16:31,990
I just saw Cathy on Tuesday.

208
00:16:32,025 --> 00:16:34,069
Are you okay?

209
00:16:34,093 --> 00:16:35,237
I honestly don't know

210
00:16:35,261 --> 00:16:36,772
what I'm going to
do without her, Grant.

211
00:16:36,796 --> 00:16:38,407
I'll miss her.

212
00:16:38,431 --> 00:16:40,497
Cathy deserved better.

213
00:16:43,336 --> 00:16:45,369
I'd like to offer
our condolences.

214
00:16:45,405 --> 00:16:47,549
I'm Michelle Thomas,
Ben Matlock's associate.

215
00:16:47,573 --> 00:16:49,039
This is Conrad McMasters.

216
00:16:49,074 --> 00:16:50,775
We represent Mr. Howell.

217
00:16:50,810 --> 00:16:51,987
Thank you, Miss Thomas.

218
00:16:52,011 --> 00:16:54,445
I understand Mrs. Gordon
was a lovely woman.

219
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:55,913
More than lovely, Mr...

220
00:16:55,948 --> 00:16:57,281
McMasters.

221
00:16:57,316 --> 00:16:59,396
She was the finest
woman I've ever known.

222
00:17:00,319 --> 00:17:01,385
Excuse me.

223
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:03,287
I need a glass of water.

224
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:10,761
My wife and Cathy
were very close.

225
00:17:10,796 --> 00:17:12,530
I'm Grant Estes.

226
00:17:12,565 --> 00:17:14,676
Glad to meet you.
How do you do? Hello.

227
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:17,146
Alex?

228
00:17:17,170 --> 00:17:18,970
I know I shouldn't have
come here, but please,

229
00:17:19,005 --> 00:17:20,615
you've got to believe me.

230
00:17:20,639 --> 00:17:22,273
I didn't kill Cathy.

231
00:17:22,308 --> 00:17:23,308
Believe you?

232
00:17:23,342 --> 00:17:25,410
You two-faced bastard.

233
00:17:25,445 --> 00:17:26,789
Alex... Sleeping with my wife,

234
00:17:26,813 --> 00:17:28,624
pretending to be my best friend.

235
00:17:28,648 --> 00:17:31,248
Get the hell out of my house!

236
00:17:59,812 --> 00:18:01,645
Nice outfit.

237
00:18:03,382 --> 00:18:04,748
Hey.

238
00:18:06,118 --> 00:18:08,285
Very impressive.

239
00:18:11,724 --> 00:18:13,157
Great stress release.

240
00:18:13,192 --> 00:18:15,459
Three times a
week, no matter what.

241
00:18:15,494 --> 00:18:17,127
Oh.

242
00:18:18,797 --> 00:18:21,732
I... I've got some
dumbbells in my den.

243
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:23,067
Christmas present.

244
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:25,214
I guess somebody's
trying to tell me something.

245
00:18:25,238 --> 00:18:26,636
Yep.

246
00:18:26,672 --> 00:18:28,016
Yeah.

247
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,373
Yeah, I...

248
00:18:29,408 --> 00:18:30,875
I try sometimes,

249
00:18:30,910 --> 00:18:32,420
but I'll do... I'll do better.

250
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:34,923
But, boy, your upper body...

251
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:37,314
My upper body's all I've got.

252
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:43,553
Um, uh...

253
00:18:43,589 --> 00:18:46,790
I, uh... I-I-I
promised I'd do this.

254
00:18:46,825 --> 00:18:49,093
Uh... um...

255
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:53,230
why I'm here is, um,
my client would-would...

256
00:18:53,266 --> 00:18:55,577
would like to
come to the funeral.

257
00:18:58,670 --> 00:19:00,138
He's out of his mind.

258
00:19:00,173 --> 00:19:02,006
Keep him away from me.

259
00:19:03,742 --> 00:19:06,777
I'm... I'm sorry I
interrupted your workout.

260
00:19:08,581 --> 00:19:09,847
That's okay.

261
00:19:13,419 --> 00:19:16,954
Um, Bret... Bret
said that he kept

262
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:20,524
an extra set of car
keys in his, uh...

263
00:19:20,559 --> 00:19:22,326
uh, desk in his office.

264
00:19:22,361 --> 00:19:24,173
You didn't happen
to see anybody...

265
00:19:24,197 --> 00:19:26,464
No, I didn't.

266
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:29,300
So, you-you think the
dumbbells would help, huh?

267
00:19:30,403 --> 00:19:31,935
It's a start.

268
00:19:31,971 --> 00:19:33,937
You could lose some weight, too.

269
00:19:35,041 --> 00:19:36,674
You think so?

270
00:19:36,709 --> 00:19:39,076
Well, you carry all that
stuff around with you,

271
00:19:39,111 --> 00:19:40,923
you probably don't
feel like exercising.

272
00:19:40,947 --> 00:19:44,549
Oh, well, I'll-I'll...
I'll do better.

273
00:19:44,584 --> 00:19:47,585
You know what they
say: we are what we eat.

274
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:49,820
On you, it shows.

275
00:19:53,092 --> 00:19:54,825
Well, uh...

276
00:20:08,507 --> 00:20:11,053
So, what can I do for
you, Miss Thomas?

277
00:20:11,077 --> 00:20:14,045
You and Cathy Gordon
were friends for quite a while.

278
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,813
Since high school.

279
00:20:15,848 --> 00:20:18,288
Did you and your husband spend
a lot of time with the Gordons?

280
00:20:19,819 --> 00:20:22,220
I spent a lot of
time with Cathy.

281
00:20:22,255 --> 00:20:23,354
And Alex?

282
00:20:23,389 --> 00:20:25,923
No, I avoided Alex
as much as I could.

283
00:20:25,958 --> 00:20:27,258
Oh?

284
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:32,296
Life's too short to be
around nasty people.

285
00:20:32,332 --> 00:20:33,965
He made Cathy miserable.

286
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,734
Well, yesterday, he sounded
like he loved her very much.

287
00:20:39,806 --> 00:20:41,538
It's an act.

288
00:20:42,642 --> 00:20:44,408
Well, did Cathy love him?

289
00:20:44,443 --> 00:20:46,177
She tried to be very loyal.

290
00:20:48,013 --> 00:20:50,147
Was there any...

291
00:20:51,751 --> 00:20:53,718
Well, I mean, could... could he?

292
00:20:53,753 --> 00:20:55,786
Yes, he could.

293
00:20:55,822 --> 00:20:57,788
And he wouldn't.

294
00:20:57,823 --> 00:20:59,222
Why wouldn't he?

295
00:21:02,361 --> 00:21:04,261
Uh... anger.

296
00:21:04,297 --> 00:21:05,930
Anger, I guess.

297
00:21:09,702 --> 00:21:11,268
How did it happen?

298
00:21:12,671 --> 00:21:15,372
One night, Cathy was driving
them home from a party.

299
00:21:15,407 --> 00:21:18,476
She got cut off, lost
control of the car, it rolled.

300
00:21:18,511 --> 00:21:21,612
Alex was thrown clear,
but Cathy got trapped.

301
00:21:21,647 --> 00:21:25,416
The car caught fire.

302
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:28,252
Somehow, Alex
managed to pull her out,

303
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:30,154
but the car lurched,

304
00:21:30,189 --> 00:21:34,458
and Alex suffered a
serious spinal injury.

305
00:21:34,494 --> 00:21:38,462
It put stress on a marriage
that wasn't good to begin with.

306
00:21:39,565 --> 00:21:40,776
Miss Thomas,

307
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,266
this is only me talking.

308
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:45,535
Before the accident, Alex
Gordon was not a nice person.

309
00:21:45,571 --> 00:21:48,672
Being paralyzed did not
improve his personality.

310
00:21:50,109 --> 00:21:52,209
He used Cathy's guilt,

311
00:21:52,245 --> 00:21:54,712
and he would never
ask for a divorce.

312
00:21:54,747 --> 00:21:55,946
Why wouldn't he?

313
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:57,559
He made six figures.

314
00:21:57,583 --> 00:21:59,561
She inherited $6 million.

315
00:21:59,585 --> 00:22:01,886
That's the difference
between comfort and luxury.

316
00:22:01,921 --> 00:22:04,722
Did Alex know
about Cathy's affair?

317
00:22:06,392 --> 00:22:09,326
I didn't think so.

318
00:22:09,361 --> 00:22:11,328
Cathy told me.

319
00:22:13,933 --> 00:22:17,868
She... she felt so guilty.

320
00:22:22,675 --> 00:22:24,041
Miss Thomas,

321
00:22:24,076 --> 00:22:28,211
whatever happiness Cathy
had, she had with Bret Howell.

322
00:22:28,247 --> 00:22:31,582
She loved him, and
he loved her very much.

323
00:22:33,986 --> 00:22:35,553
Come on, Ben,
there's just no way

324
00:22:35,588 --> 00:22:37,332
a paraplegic could have
committed that murder.

325
00:22:37,356 --> 00:22:39,190
I didn't say he did.

326
00:22:39,225 --> 00:22:41,225
I just want to find
out more about him

327
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:43,661
and about the motel
where he stayed that night.

328
00:22:43,696 --> 00:22:47,230
Eh... unless the man is cured
and nobody knows about it,

329
00:22:47,266 --> 00:22:49,800
I... think you're barking
up the wrong tree.

330
00:22:49,835 --> 00:22:51,480
You want to just
find out something

331
00:22:51,504 --> 00:22:53,837
about the motel where
he stayed that night?

332
00:22:56,174 --> 00:22:58,275
I'll find out about the motel.

333
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:03,658
Barking up the wrong tree.

334
00:23:37,182 --> 00:23:39,216
Man, you scared
the devil out of me.

335
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:40,885
Here, let me give you a hand

336
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:42,286
with that. No, no.

337
00:23:42,321 --> 00:23:43,621
Thanks.

338
00:23:43,656 --> 00:23:44,722
Okay.

339
00:23:44,757 --> 00:23:46,757
I have plenty to do.

340
00:24:00,105 --> 00:24:01,838
Lunch.

341
00:24:01,874 --> 00:24:03,173
What do you got?

342
00:24:03,208 --> 00:24:06,443
Ooh... I got two
hamburgers jumbo,

343
00:24:06,478 --> 00:24:08,690
two hot dogs all the way.

344
00:24:08,714 --> 00:24:12,049
I got fries, onion
rings, rice pudding,

345
00:24:12,084 --> 00:24:15,886
and two milkshakes... vanilla...
And one extra just in case.

346
00:24:17,456 --> 00:24:18,489
What's the matter?

347
00:24:18,524 --> 00:24:20,090
Nothing.

348
00:24:20,125 --> 00:24:21,358
You like hot dogs.

349
00:24:21,393 --> 00:24:22,793
Yeah.

350
00:24:22,828 --> 00:24:25,462
Well, what's the matter?

351
00:24:25,498 --> 00:24:27,898
Well... somebody said

352
00:24:27,933 --> 00:24:30,434
maybe I ought to
lose a little weight.

353
00:24:33,038 --> 00:24:36,407
What do you think?

354
00:24:36,442 --> 00:24:37,741
You're plump.

355
00:24:38,844 --> 00:24:40,845
Pleasingly plump?

356
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:42,212
Just plump.

357
00:24:44,716 --> 00:24:47,685
Well... diet then.

358
00:24:47,720 --> 00:24:50,654
I can't be losing my figure.

359
00:24:50,690 --> 00:24:55,258
That used to be one
of my best things.

360
00:24:55,294 --> 00:24:57,327
You know that motel
you told me to look into?

361
00:24:57,362 --> 00:24:58,528
Yeah.

362
00:24:58,564 --> 00:25:00,831
Well, Alex Gordon always
stays in the same room

363
00:25:00,866 --> 00:25:02,900
because it has easy
wheelchair access.

364
00:25:02,935 --> 00:25:04,267
Yeah.

365
00:25:04,303 --> 00:25:07,171
I don't know what this means,
but the night of the murder,

366
00:25:07,206 --> 00:25:10,107
he said he wanted a quiet
room because he was real tired,

367
00:25:10,142 --> 00:25:12,142
even though the
access was more difficult.

368
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:14,712
They saw him check in,
they saw him check out.

369
00:25:14,747 --> 00:25:17,781
But in between, he could
have gone anywhere.

370
00:25:17,817 --> 00:25:19,650
Like I said, I don't
know what that means

371
00:25:19,685 --> 00:25:21,885
because I found out this.

372
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,319
Man makes a good living, right?

373
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:25,400
But his wife is the
one with all the money.

374
00:25:25,424 --> 00:25:28,392
Well, that's reason
enough to kill her right there.

375
00:25:28,427 --> 00:25:30,861
Yeah, but except for
token maintenance,

376
00:25:30,897 --> 00:25:33,063
Alex Gordon is
not in his wife's will.

377
00:25:33,098 --> 00:25:34,898
He's not?

378
00:25:34,934 --> 00:25:36,233
How'd you find out?

379
00:25:36,268 --> 00:25:37,434
Connections.

380
00:25:37,469 --> 00:25:38,569
Does he know?

381
00:25:38,604 --> 00:25:40,571
Contact says yes.

382
00:25:40,606 --> 00:25:43,006
Huh.

383
00:25:43,042 --> 00:25:46,677
Well, the only way he could
get any of her money was

384
00:25:46,712 --> 00:25:48,144
if she was alive.

385
00:25:48,180 --> 00:25:49,145
Doesn't make any sense.

386
00:25:49,181 --> 00:25:50,347
Nope.

387
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:53,050
I think you're barking
up the wrong tree.

388
00:25:54,153 --> 00:25:57,954
Wrong tree, huh?

389
00:25:57,990 --> 00:26:01,392
I want you to follow
him everywhere.

390
00:26:03,495 --> 00:26:07,965
Okay, got my
stuff, got my radio.

391
00:26:09,034 --> 00:26:10,534
You gonna eat those hot dogs?

392
00:26:10,569 --> 00:26:11,535
Yes.

393
00:26:11,570 --> 00:26:12,536
Both of 'em?

394
00:26:12,571 --> 00:26:14,238
Yes. When?

395
00:26:14,273 --> 00:26:17,074
While I'm working,
following Alex Gordon.

396
00:26:19,178 --> 00:26:21,711
Well, what are you gonna
do with all that other stuff?

397
00:26:22,815 --> 00:26:25,448
I'm gonna eat it.

398
00:26:30,923 --> 00:26:32,389
I knew it was 8:30

399
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:34,536
because that's when I
walk Jerome every night.

400
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:36,393
Jerome is my dog.

401
00:26:36,428 --> 00:26:40,497
Anyway, I noticed this burgundy
Jaguar parked near my house.

402
00:26:40,533 --> 00:26:42,833
When I looked around
to see who it belonged to,

403
00:26:42,868 --> 00:26:45,536
I noticed someone going
into the Gordons' house.

404
00:26:45,571 --> 00:26:47,404
And what exactly did you see?

405
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:51,375
Well, Mrs. Gordon sort
of pulled this man inside.

406
00:26:51,410 --> 00:26:53,410
Do you see the
person who was pulled

407
00:26:53,445 --> 00:26:55,056
into the Gordons'
house here today?

408
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:57,313
Sure, I've seen
him there before.

409
00:26:57,349 --> 00:26:58,515
The defendant

410
00:26:58,550 --> 00:27:00,818
Mr. Howell.

411
00:27:00,853 --> 00:27:03,987
In all of the years I've
worked for the Gordons,

412
00:27:04,023 --> 00:27:07,291
the alarm was always
on when I went to work.

413
00:27:07,326 --> 00:27:10,360
Mrs. Gordon simply
never would go to sleep

414
00:27:10,395 --> 00:27:11,695
without turning it on.

415
00:27:11,730 --> 00:27:12,962
Never?

416
00:27:12,998 --> 00:27:16,166
Not even if she was sick or
injured or just plain forgot?

417
00:27:16,201 --> 00:27:17,735
No, never.

418
00:27:17,770 --> 00:27:22,706
So, if Mrs. Gordon had been
alive when the defendant left,

419
00:27:22,742 --> 00:27:24,742
she would have
turned the alarm on,

420
00:27:24,777 --> 00:27:26,387
and therefore no one
could enter the house

421
00:27:26,411 --> 00:27:27,678
without setting it off?

422
00:27:27,713 --> 00:27:29,413
No one.

423
00:27:29,448 --> 00:27:32,148
Thank you very much.

424
00:27:32,183 --> 00:27:33,350
No questions.

425
00:27:33,385 --> 00:27:35,119
Mr. Matlock.

426
00:27:35,154 --> 00:27:36,520
No questions.

427
00:27:36,555 --> 00:27:37,655
You may step down.

428
00:27:37,690 --> 00:27:39,289
Court will recess

429
00:27:39,324 --> 00:27:40,769
45 minutes for lunch.

430
00:27:56,008 --> 00:27:57,707
Uh, M-Mr. Gordon?

431
00:27:57,743 --> 00:27:58,875
Yeah?

432
00:27:58,910 --> 00:28:03,213
Uh, uh, this...
this may, uh, uh,

433
00:28:03,249 --> 00:28:04,426
be a little awkward,

434
00:28:04,450 --> 00:28:06,227
but I'll just go ahead with it.

435
00:28:06,251 --> 00:28:09,019
Bret said that, uh,
you stayed in town

436
00:28:09,054 --> 00:28:10,465
the night of the
murder and worked

437
00:28:10,489 --> 00:28:15,059
on the Uniwear campaign,
and, uh, the meeting's next week,

438
00:28:15,094 --> 00:28:17,728
and if you have the
campaign, he'd like to present it.

439
00:28:17,763 --> 00:28:20,864
Tell Bret to stick it.

440
00:28:20,899 --> 00:28:22,833
Okay.

441
00:28:22,868 --> 00:28:25,601
Uh, why didn't you stay

442
00:28:25,637 --> 00:28:28,016
in your regular room
at the motel that night?

443
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:29,739
The front room is noisy.

444
00:28:30,775 --> 00:28:32,954
I need quiet to work and sleep.

445
00:28:32,978 --> 00:28:34,244
I see, hmm,

446
00:28:34,279 --> 00:28:37,814
I see.

447
00:28:37,850 --> 00:28:40,217
You think I'm a suspect?

448
00:28:42,387 --> 00:28:44,387
Well, I'll take that
as a compliment.

449
00:28:45,591 --> 00:28:49,159
You think I snuck out
and murdered my wife

450
00:28:49,194 --> 00:28:51,327
in my wheelchair?

451
00:28:51,363 --> 00:28:54,197
Mr. Matlock.

452
00:28:56,268 --> 00:28:59,103
<i>Numerous places</i>

453
00:28:59,138 --> 00:29:02,038
in the victim's bedroom and
the entire house were dusted.

454
00:29:02,074 --> 00:29:03,574
And what did you find?

455
00:29:03,609 --> 00:29:05,787
We found the fingerprints
of the defendant, Mr. Howell,

456
00:29:05,811 --> 00:29:06,944
throughout the house

457
00:29:06,979 --> 00:29:09,646
and in particular, in
the victim's bedroom.

458
00:29:09,681 --> 00:29:10,980
Thank you.

459
00:29:11,016 --> 00:29:11,981
Nothing further.

460
00:29:12,017 --> 00:29:13,961
Mr. Matlock. Yes, sir.

461
00:29:13,985 --> 00:29:18,855
Uh, Lieutenant... do
you from time to time, uh,

462
00:29:18,890 --> 00:29:21,625
visit with friends and
business associates

463
00:29:21,660 --> 00:29:23,961
at, uh, their various homes?

464
00:29:23,996 --> 00:29:25,529
Yes. Well,

465
00:29:25,564 --> 00:29:27,731
when you take
leave of one another,

466
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:29,933
uh, do you take care

467
00:29:29,968 --> 00:29:32,669
to wipe your fingerprints
off everything...

468
00:29:32,704 --> 00:29:36,940
Uh, uh, tableware, tables
and the walls and stuff like that?

469
00:29:36,975 --> 00:29:38,075
No.

470
00:29:38,110 --> 00:29:39,776
Yes.

471
00:29:39,811 --> 00:29:42,512
Now, you've testified

472
00:29:42,548 --> 00:29:45,815
that this knife is
the murder weapon

473
00:29:45,850 --> 00:29:49,086
and that it was found in
the trunk of Mr. Howell's car?

474
00:29:49,121 --> 00:29:50,687
Yes, sir.

475
00:29:50,722 --> 00:29:54,124
Well, why are there
no fingerprints on it?

476
00:29:54,159 --> 00:29:55,692
Well... LLOYD: Objection.

477
00:29:55,727 --> 00:29:57,071
- Calls for speculation.
- Sustained.

478
00:29:57,095 --> 00:29:58,806
It doesn't make sense
that-that... Mr. Matlock.

479
00:29:58,830 --> 00:30:00,897
That the defendant
would leave his fingerprints

480
00:30:00,932 --> 00:30:02,777
Mr. Matlock. all over
the walls of the house

481
00:30:02,801 --> 00:30:04,111
and wipe 'em off
the knife Mr. Matlock.

482
00:30:04,135 --> 00:30:05,647
Before he threw it
in the trunk of his car.

483
00:30:05,671 --> 00:30:07,248
Sustained. LLOYD:
Objection. It's argumentative.

484
00:30:07,272 --> 00:30:09,184
Sustained. Well, why-why
didn't he just leave the knife

485
00:30:09,208 --> 00:30:10,451
at the scene of the
crime? Mr. Matlock.

486
00:30:10,475 --> 00:30:11,986
You'll have to ask your
client. Or whoever committed

487
00:30:12,010 --> 00:30:13,387
this horrible
murder. Mr. Matlock.

488
00:30:13,411 --> 00:30:14,377
Withdraw the question.

489
00:30:14,412 --> 00:30:15,623
Nothing further.

490
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:17,559
We'll adjourn till 10:00
tomorrow morning.

491
00:30:18,717 --> 00:30:19,783
Uh, Your Honor,

492
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:21,017
Your Honor, Your Honor,

493
00:30:21,052 --> 00:30:24,621
could counsel and I meet
with you in chambers briefly?

494
00:30:24,656 --> 00:30:26,934
Mr. Burgess?

495
00:30:26,958 --> 00:30:27,924
That's fine, yes, sir.

496
00:30:27,959 --> 00:30:28,970
And-and could we ask

497
00:30:28,994 --> 00:30:30,561
Mr. Alex Gordon

498
00:30:30,596 --> 00:30:33,630
to meet with us?

499
00:30:33,665 --> 00:30:37,967
Your Honor, this is a receipt
for a $50,000 diamond bracelet

500
00:30:38,003 --> 00:30:42,072
that my client gave the deceased
the day before she was murdered.

501
00:30:42,107 --> 00:30:43,818
What's the point? Well,

502
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:45,676
the bracelet hasn't shown up

503
00:30:45,711 --> 00:30:48,578
anywhere in Mrs.
Gordon's possessions,

504
00:30:48,614 --> 00:30:50,948
and I'd like to search the safes

505
00:30:50,983 --> 00:30:52,916
up in her bedroom
to see if it's there.

506
00:30:52,951 --> 00:30:54,484
For what purpose?

507
00:30:54,520 --> 00:30:55,686
Y-You said that

508
00:30:55,721 --> 00:30:58,454
no robbery was
involved in this murder,

509
00:30:58,490 --> 00:31:03,326
and if the bracelet isn't
there, it proves that there was.

510
00:31:03,361 --> 00:31:06,363
Mr. Matlock, if you're
introducing evidence,

511
00:31:06,398 --> 00:31:09,066
you must do so in a
courtroom, and if you're asking

512
00:31:09,101 --> 00:31:11,268
for a warrant to search
the Gordon house,

513
00:31:11,303 --> 00:31:13,303
then ask right now.

514
00:31:13,338 --> 00:31:14,872
Well, um...

515
00:31:14,907 --> 00:31:18,308
I have no problem with
your going into the safe.

516
00:31:18,344 --> 00:31:20,021
Come by first
thing in the morning.

517
00:31:20,045 --> 00:31:22,179
You can look
around all you want.

518
00:31:35,827 --> 00:31:37,794
This it?

519
00:31:37,829 --> 00:31:39,496
Hmm.

520
00:31:39,531 --> 00:31:42,132
It sure looks like it.

521
00:31:42,167 --> 00:31:43,333
Yeah, that's got

522
00:31:43,368 --> 00:31:45,335
to be it.

523
00:31:45,370 --> 00:31:48,705
Well, it looks like you missed
this one, doesn't it, Ben?

524
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:51,441
Oh. Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

525
00:31:51,476 --> 00:31:54,210
Nice try, Ben.

526
00:32:02,888 --> 00:32:04,054
Yeah.

527
00:32:04,089 --> 00:32:05,255
Yeah, that's right.

528
00:32:09,928 --> 00:32:11,406
You find what you
were looking for?

529
00:32:11,430 --> 00:32:14,764
Uh, yes. I-I'll be right
with you, be right there.

530
00:32:14,799 --> 00:32:16,500
Yes, we did.

531
00:32:16,535 --> 00:32:19,503
Uh...

532
00:32:19,538 --> 00:32:22,705
Mr. Gordon, um...

533
00:32:22,741 --> 00:32:24,674
how are you doing?

534
00:32:25,777 --> 00:32:28,511
I miss my wife...

535
00:32:28,547 --> 00:32:31,948
more than I can
say, but I'm all right.

536
00:32:31,983 --> 00:32:34,684
I trained myself early
to be self-sufficient.

537
00:32:34,720 --> 00:32:37,721
I-I didn't want to be
a burden to Cathy.

538
00:32:37,756 --> 00:32:41,791
I'm moved by your
internal strength.

539
00:32:41,827 --> 00:32:45,195
Paralyzed when you
saved your wife's life,

540
00:32:45,230 --> 00:32:46,495
and now to find out...

541
00:32:46,531 --> 00:32:48,509
I'm a practical
man, Mr. Matlock.

542
00:32:48,533 --> 00:32:51,468
I understood my wife's needs.

543
00:32:51,503 --> 00:32:55,806
I couldn't fulfill all of
them... most but not all.

544
00:32:55,841 --> 00:32:57,341
That's more than practical.

545
00:32:57,376 --> 00:33:00,076
I'll be honest with
you, Mr. Matlock.

546
00:33:00,111 --> 00:33:03,814
At first I felt
rage, bitterness.

547
00:33:03,849 --> 00:33:06,282
Life isn't fair, I know it,

548
00:33:06,318 --> 00:33:09,453
but I also know that if the
situation had been reversed,

549
00:33:09,488 --> 00:33:11,333
Cathy would have
pulled me out of that car

550
00:33:11,357 --> 00:33:14,891
and eventually I might
have had an affair.

551
00:33:14,926 --> 00:33:18,395
Well...

552
00:33:18,430 --> 00:33:21,498
I wish life had turned
out differently for you.

553
00:33:21,533 --> 00:33:22,499
Thank you.

554
00:33:22,534 --> 00:33:24,601
Yes.

555
00:33:28,339 --> 00:33:30,507
It's-it's a very nice house.

556
00:33:30,542 --> 00:33:32,008
Yes, it is.

557
00:33:32,043 --> 00:33:34,677
I may keep it, I don't know.

558
00:33:34,713 --> 00:33:36,680
Expensive to keep up.

559
00:33:39,351 --> 00:33:41,584
Well...

560
00:33:42,987 --> 00:33:44,921
Uh...

561
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:49,993
Um...

562
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:52,128
What?

563
00:33:54,232 --> 00:33:58,134
There's, uh, there's something

564
00:33:58,170 --> 00:34:01,871
you probably don't know about.

565
00:34:03,141 --> 00:34:06,309
Your wife gave Mr. Howell

566
00:34:06,344 --> 00:34:08,912
the combination to
your upstairs safe,

567
00:34:08,947 --> 00:34:13,350
and so the other
day I took a little look.

568
00:34:13,385 --> 00:34:17,086
I might get in trouble,
I don't know, but...

569
00:34:17,121 --> 00:34:21,558
funny thing... The
bracelet wasn't there.

570
00:34:21,593 --> 00:34:22,926
I'm certain of it.

571
00:34:22,961 --> 00:34:25,862
And then remember in chambers

572
00:34:25,898 --> 00:34:28,965
we asked if we could...
we could take a look

573
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:31,446
and you said fine, remember,
and we just did, we just looked,

574
00:34:31,470 --> 00:34:36,206
and... the bracelet is there.

575
00:34:36,241 --> 00:34:38,608
It's there.

576
00:34:41,846 --> 00:34:45,348
And, uh...

577
00:34:45,384 --> 00:34:47,317
I don't understand.

578
00:34:49,387 --> 00:34:52,656
Well... I'll go.

579
00:35:57,088 --> 00:35:59,066
May I have your order, please?

580
00:35:59,090 --> 00:36:02,926
Hi. Give me a chocolate
shake and a hamburger.

581
00:36:42,600 --> 00:36:44,367
Ben Matlock.

582
00:36:44,402 --> 00:36:47,636
Ben, I'm at a drive-through
on East Magnolia.

583
00:36:47,672 --> 00:36:49,638
He lost me.

584
00:37:21,606 --> 00:37:23,907
<i>Mr. Gordon,</i>

585
00:37:23,942 --> 00:37:26,009
I know this will
be difficult for you,

586
00:37:26,044 --> 00:37:28,611
but I'd like to talk about

587
00:37:28,646 --> 00:37:31,881
your relationship
with your wife.

588
00:37:33,651 --> 00:37:36,318
Uh, was there intimacy?

589
00:37:37,422 --> 00:37:40,523
That was impossible.

590
00:37:40,558 --> 00:37:43,893
I have been told
just the opposite.

591
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:45,862
That it's very possible.

592
00:37:48,867 --> 00:37:50,834
Were you happy?

593
00:37:50,869 --> 00:37:53,214
Happier than most marriages.

594
00:37:53,238 --> 00:37:56,573
Well, you know that your
wife was in love with my client?

595
00:37:56,608 --> 00:37:59,587
An affair is not
love, Mr. Matlock.

596
00:37:59,611 --> 00:38:02,511
My wife and I understood
each other's needs,

597
00:38:02,547 --> 00:38:03,824
and we accepted them.

598
00:38:03,848 --> 00:38:06,416
That was one of the
strengths of our marriage.

599
00:38:06,451 --> 00:38:10,120
Well, Mrs. Gordon was planning
to divorce you, wasn't she?

600
00:38:10,155 --> 00:38:13,923
Like any couple that's been
married longer than two weeks,

601
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:16,137
we'd occasionally
discuss divorce

602
00:38:16,161 --> 00:38:17,905
in the heat of an argument.

603
00:38:17,929 --> 00:38:19,161
Uh-huh.

604
00:38:19,197 --> 00:38:21,431
Do you know a man
named Mr. Martin Sedgwick?

605
00:38:21,466 --> 00:38:23,466
Yes, I do. He's an attorney.

606
00:38:23,501 --> 00:38:28,004
In fact, he is the
attorney your wife retained

607
00:38:28,039 --> 00:38:30,873
to file for divorce
in her behalf.

608
00:38:30,908 --> 00:38:32,142
Isn't that right?

609
00:38:32,177 --> 00:38:33,510
She hired him, yes,

610
00:38:33,545 --> 00:38:35,845
but she never would
have gone through with it.

611
00:38:36,948 --> 00:38:39,049
Because she loved you?

612
00:38:39,084 --> 00:38:40,750
Yes.

613
00:38:40,785 --> 00:38:42,352
Cathy was hot-tempered

614
00:38:42,387 --> 00:38:44,587
and certainly had a
flair for the dramatic.

615
00:38:44,622 --> 00:38:46,800
Instead of saying, "I'm angry,"

616
00:38:46,824 --> 00:38:48,335
she'd file for divorce.

617
00:38:48,359 --> 00:38:51,194
But that was one of the
things I loved about her.

618
00:38:51,229 --> 00:38:54,164
I'm easily bored, Mr. Matlock,

619
00:38:54,199 --> 00:38:56,199
and Cathy was never boring.

620
00:38:56,234 --> 00:38:58,201
You miss her.

621
00:38:58,236 --> 00:39:00,570
Yes. Very much.

622
00:39:02,607 --> 00:39:05,808
Your wife's family inheritance

623
00:39:05,843 --> 00:39:08,078
allowed a lifestyle

624
00:39:08,113 --> 00:39:10,646
that, uh, your salary
alone could never support.

625
00:39:10,682 --> 00:39:11,915
Isn't that right?

626
00:39:11,950 --> 00:39:13,182
That's insulting.

627
00:39:13,218 --> 00:39:15,251
Objection! Relevancy.

628
00:39:15,286 --> 00:39:17,954
Mr. Matlock, this man
is not on trial here.

629
00:39:17,989 --> 00:39:19,155
Your client is.

630
00:39:19,190 --> 00:39:20,868
Your Honor... I'm sustaining

631
00:39:20,892 --> 00:39:22,124
the objection, Mr. Matlock.

632
00:39:22,160 --> 00:39:23,259
Move on.

633
00:39:24,996 --> 00:39:26,996
The night

634
00:39:27,031 --> 00:39:29,632
your wife was murdered,

635
00:39:29,668 --> 00:39:32,335
you stayed in town
in a motel, didn't you?

636
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:33,670
Yes.

637
00:39:33,705 --> 00:39:36,673
And you always stay in the
same motel in the same room

638
00:39:36,708 --> 00:39:38,407
because it has
wheelchair access.

639
00:39:38,443 --> 00:39:41,478
But this night, you stayed in
a different room, didn't you?

640
00:39:41,513 --> 00:39:42,657
I was tired.

641
00:39:42,681 --> 00:39:44,892
My regular room is
right next to the office.

642
00:39:44,916 --> 00:39:46,293
Can be quite noisy sometimes.

643
00:39:46,317 --> 00:39:47,895
I told you that
already, remember?

644
00:39:47,919 --> 00:39:52,422
The room you stayed in
was way in back of the motel.

645
00:39:52,457 --> 00:39:56,526
The manager helped you
check in, helped you check out.

646
00:39:56,561 --> 00:39:58,762
But in the meantime,

647
00:39:58,797 --> 00:40:01,030
given the location of the room,

648
00:40:01,065 --> 00:40:02,899
you could have gone
somewhere, come back,

649
00:40:02,934 --> 00:40:04,601
never been seen, couldn't you?

650
00:40:04,636 --> 00:40:07,114
I stayed in that room all night.

651
00:40:07,138 --> 00:40:08,816
Mr. Gordon,

652
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:10,807
you have

653
00:40:10,842 --> 00:40:13,042
tremendous upper
body strength, don't you?

654
00:40:13,077 --> 00:40:14,544
Yes.

655
00:40:14,579 --> 00:40:16,790
You would, too, if
you had to drag around

656
00:40:16,814 --> 00:40:18,292
half a body of dead weight.

657
00:40:18,316 --> 00:40:21,484
You lift weights? Yes.

658
00:40:21,519 --> 00:40:25,221
Could you climb up a rope?

659
00:40:27,926 --> 00:40:29,893
I've never tried.

660
00:40:29,928 --> 00:40:31,928
I'd have to say no.

661
00:40:31,963 --> 00:40:33,897
Feet are part of the power.

662
00:40:33,932 --> 00:40:37,533
But given the tremendous
upper body strength you have,

663
00:40:37,568 --> 00:40:41,037
wouldn't it be
fairly easy for you?

664
00:40:41,072 --> 00:40:44,240
Nothing is easy for a
paraplegic, Mr. Matlock.

665
00:40:44,275 --> 00:40:46,209
Let me tell you a story.

666
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:52,048
There was a man

667
00:40:52,083 --> 00:40:55,084
who was filled with rage.

668
00:40:57,956 --> 00:41:00,456
And he was victim of an accident

669
00:41:00,491 --> 00:41:03,126
that left him paralyzed.

670
00:41:03,161 --> 00:41:05,094
A terrible loss.

671
00:41:07,298 --> 00:41:10,699
And his rage built more rage.

672
00:41:10,735 --> 00:41:13,102
Maybe even pathological.

673
00:41:16,340 --> 00:41:18,274
Many, many people,

674
00:41:18,309 --> 00:41:20,609
disabled just like he,

675
00:41:20,645 --> 00:41:23,479
work their way
through their loss,

676
00:41:23,514 --> 00:41:25,748
and live their lives.

677
00:41:25,784 --> 00:41:27,750
Productive.

678
00:41:29,220 --> 00:41:33,089
But rage had always
been a part of this man,

679
00:41:33,124 --> 00:41:36,525
and now it was his
constant companion.

680
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:37,805
So one night,

681
00:41:37,829 --> 00:41:39,829
he called his wife

682
00:41:39,864 --> 00:41:41,708
and told her he was
gonna stay in town,

683
00:41:41,732 --> 00:41:45,601
knowing that his
business partner

684
00:41:45,636 --> 00:41:48,337
would take that
opportunity to see her.

685
00:41:48,372 --> 00:41:50,173
An affair.

686
00:41:50,208 --> 00:41:53,075
An affair, perhaps brought on

687
00:41:53,111 --> 00:41:55,812
by the numerous
rejections of the husband.

688
00:41:55,847 --> 00:41:59,115
And he knew that his
neighbor would walk his dog

689
00:41:59,150 --> 00:42:01,217
at the same time every night

690
00:42:01,252 --> 00:42:02,751
and see his partner's car

691
00:42:02,787 --> 00:42:04,598
parked out in
front of the house.

692
00:42:04,622 --> 00:42:05,921
You are saying

693
00:42:05,957 --> 00:42:07,634
that I deliberately
set up an opportunity

694
00:42:07,658 --> 00:42:08,825
for Bret to meet Cathy?

695
00:42:08,860 --> 00:42:10,604
Just a story. LLOYD: Objection!

696
00:42:10,628 --> 00:42:13,296
Your Honor, this is crucial

697
00:42:13,331 --> 00:42:15,665
to the completion of this case.

698
00:42:15,700 --> 00:42:17,733
Careful, Mr. Matlock.

699
00:42:17,769 --> 00:42:20,269
Be very careful.

700
00:42:20,304 --> 00:42:21,670
Overruled.

701
00:42:26,544 --> 00:42:30,312
Once you had
established your alibi

702
00:42:30,347 --> 00:42:32,347
at the motel,

703
00:42:32,383 --> 00:42:34,684
you drove to your house,

704
00:42:34,719 --> 00:42:37,653
waited for your partner,
my client, to leave,

705
00:42:37,689 --> 00:42:39,355
and your wife to go to sleep.

706
00:42:39,390 --> 00:42:44,093
Then you turned off the
alarm, went in the house.

707
00:42:44,128 --> 00:42:46,930
You knew

708
00:42:46,965 --> 00:42:48,998
you could go up those stairs

709
00:42:49,034 --> 00:42:51,700
by using your hands.

710
00:42:51,736 --> 00:42:54,971
But your legs would
drag behind you,

711
00:42:55,006 --> 00:42:58,308
leaving a-a trail
of particle evidence

712
00:42:58,343 --> 00:43:00,276
that anybody could find.

713
00:43:02,414 --> 00:43:06,282
So you threw a rope
over the upstairs banister.

714
00:43:06,317 --> 00:43:09,218
And that's how you climbed

715
00:43:09,254 --> 00:43:11,287
to the second
floor of your house,

716
00:43:11,322 --> 00:43:14,123
something no one would
think a paraplegic could do.

717
00:43:14,159 --> 00:43:15,458
Then

718
00:43:15,493 --> 00:43:17,726
you stabbed your wife to death

719
00:43:17,762 --> 00:43:19,729
while she slept.

720
00:43:19,764 --> 00:43:21,130
How dare you.

721
00:43:21,165 --> 00:43:23,332
I don't climb ropes.

722
00:43:23,367 --> 00:43:24,967
<i>How dare you!</i>

723
00:43:26,070 --> 00:43:28,270
Let me show you something.

724
00:43:28,305 --> 00:43:30,339
Let me show you something.

725
00:43:30,374 --> 00:43:32,307
Let me show you this.

726
00:43:36,981 --> 00:43:38,915
Recognize this bag?

727
00:43:44,456 --> 00:43:46,989
This is the rope you used

728
00:43:47,024 --> 00:43:49,358
to climb to the second
floor of your house.

729
00:43:52,696 --> 00:43:55,197
This is the bloody
jacket you wore...

730
00:43:57,068 --> 00:43:59,469
while you stabbed
your wife to death.

731
00:43:59,504 --> 00:44:02,137
These are the gloves

732
00:44:02,173 --> 00:44:04,106
that you wiped off.

733
00:44:06,243 --> 00:44:10,213
You knew that my
associate, Conrad McMasters,

734
00:44:10,248 --> 00:44:12,760
was following you last
night, so you lost him.

735
00:44:12,784 --> 00:44:15,084
We meant for you to do that.

736
00:44:15,120 --> 00:44:17,097
Do you recognize this gentleman?

737
00:44:17,121 --> 00:44:18,832
He's a private investigator.

738
00:44:18,856 --> 00:44:20,856
I hired him to follow you,

739
00:44:20,891 --> 00:44:23,860
and he saw you go up an alley

740
00:44:23,895 --> 00:44:26,595
and throw this bag
and the contents

741
00:44:26,630 --> 00:44:28,364
in a Dumpster.

742
00:44:28,399 --> 00:44:31,834
I'm sure forensics
testing will prove

743
00:44:31,870 --> 00:44:35,605
the blood on this jacket
and in places on this rope

744
00:44:35,640 --> 00:44:37,573
is your wife's blood.

745
00:44:44,616 --> 00:44:46,949
Millions of people
have been disabled

746
00:44:46,984 --> 00:44:50,586
like you, and have found a way

747
00:44:50,621 --> 00:44:55,658
to live fulfilling,
productive lives.

748
00:44:55,693 --> 00:44:57,826
I'm sorry for your accident,

749
00:44:57,862 --> 00:45:01,297
and I'm sorry that you
had to live in that chair.

750
00:45:01,332 --> 00:45:04,834
I'm sorry most of all

751
00:45:04,869 --> 00:45:08,070
that you allowed your rage

752
00:45:08,106 --> 00:45:10,506
to cause all of this tragedy.

753
00:45:12,210 --> 00:45:15,944
But there can be no excuse
for what you have done.

754
00:45:17,048 --> 00:45:19,182
Your Honor,

755
00:45:19,217 --> 00:45:23,252
defense moves that all charges

756
00:45:23,288 --> 00:45:26,522
against my client be dropped.

757
00:45:26,557 --> 00:45:31,360
In light of the evidence, Your
Honor, the people concur.

758
00:45:31,395 --> 00:45:34,263
As does the court.

759
00:45:34,298 --> 00:45:35,764
Case dismissed.

760
00:45:35,799 --> 00:45:37,600
This court is adjourned.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
